                <pb facs="0855" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg743"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul Moffat to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bluefields</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic">March 9,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>M. Moffat reports that he has communicated department’s telegram of March 8, 8
                    p.m., to Gen. Estrada, who has submitted the proposed peace bases to Madriz by
                    telegraph, urging his acceptance.</p>
            </div>
